{"seq":29,"at":"2026-10-23","kind":"edited","target":{"type":"article","id":"a0620"},"reason":"Added the anecdote of the cup Diogenes threw away (Diogenes Laërtius VI.37) to the sentence listing his few possessions, so the new question has a sentence that gives it.","by":"fact-count-rework","changes":[{"field":"bodyEn","diff":[["=",134],["-","bag,"],["+","bag;"],["=",1],["+","he had once carried a cup too, but when he saw a boy drinking water from his hands, he threw his cup away with the words \"A child has beaten me in plainness of living.\" He "],["=",807]]},{"field":"bodyDe","diff":[["=",132],["-","Beutel,"],["+","Beutel;"],["=",1],["+","früher hatte er auch einen Becher dabei, doch als er einen Jungen aus den hohlen Händen Wasser trinken sah, warf er seinen Becher weg mit den Worten: „Ein Kind hat mich an Genügsamkeit übertroffen.“ Er "],["=",787]]},{"field":"bodyRu","diff":[["=",114],["+","когда-то "],["=",2],["+","носил с собой и чашку, но, увидев, как мальчик пьёт воду из горсти, выбросил её — лишней оказалась даже чашка: «Ребёнок превзошёл меня простотой жизни». Он "],["=",745]]}],"hash":"a36d6989199d"},
